docs/feature-inventory.md:12:| Expressions | parentheses; + - * / % and unary +/-; < <= > >=, == != === !==, !; short-circuit &&/\|\|; assignment; conditional `test ? consequent : alternate` | Numeric operators use number-hint ordinary conversion; addition converts both operands with default hint before string/numeric selection. Relational operators convert in source order with number hint, compare two strings by UTF-16 code units, otherwise compare numbers with all NaN comparisons false. Own/inherited valueOf/toString methods work on ordinary objects, arrays and functions; default ordinary objects convert through inherited Object valueOf/toString to [object Object] (numeric NaN). Boolean/String wrappers use their standard payload methods. Number wrappers return numeric payloads for default/number hints and inherited tag strings for string hints. Arrays convert through join; functions convert to exact retained source or the native form. Both operand evaluations precede coercion. === !==, truthiness and Number predicates never coerce. Conditional precedence, selected-arm evaluation and existing bounds remain unchanged. Abstract equality selectively converts at most one object with the default hint; nullish/object and object/object comparisons never coerce. No BigInt, comma, bitwise, update, compound assignment, nullish coalescing or optional chaining. |
